<details><summary>Installation and a larger-audit example</summary><p>Requires Python 3.11+. Upload the ZIP to your VPS home folder, then:</p><pre><code>mkdir -p ~/openvist-tools
python3 -m zipfile -e ~/openvist-link-auditor-self-hosted-0.4.1.zip ~/openvist-tools
cd ~/openvist-tools/openvist-link-auditor-self-hosted-0.4.1
python3 run_audit.py --deadline 600 -- https://example.com/ \
  --max-pages 200 --max-urls 1000 --delay 0.5 --output my-audit</code></pre><p>Replace example.com with a website you manage or are authorized to audit. Open my-audit.html for the visual report. Existing output names are not overwritten.</p><p>Use --max-pages and --max-urls (1–5,000), --deadline (1–86,400 seconds), --delay, --request-timeout and --byte-limit to tune the workload. The downloadable guide explains defaults, ranges, exit codes and larger examples. Increase limits to suit your VPS resources and the destination’s request policy.</p></details></section>
<section class="ovt-notes"><h2>Clear limits. Useful results.</h2><p>Each audit checks up to 50 URLs, discovers up to 200 URLs and runs for at most 120 seconds after ownership verification. HTTPS and same-origin links only; redirects away from that origin are recorded without following them. We respect robots.txt and do not execute JavaScript or submit forms.</p><p>Three audits and three verification attempts per account in a rolling 24 hours, three active websites and 15 minutes between audits of the same website. The free beta also has a shared service capacity, so submissions may pause when it is reached.</p><p>Unchecked URLs are not failures. HTTP 200 does not confirm correct content or Google indexability. Restricted access and rate limits are reported separately. This is a bounded link check, not a complete SEO or security audit.</p></section>
<section class="ovt-notes"><h2>Private reports. Open code.</h2><p>This server tool sends your website origin and verification request to WordPress and the OpenViST VPS. Website records expire after seven days, unverified challenges after one day, and jobs and reports after 24 hours. Cleanup runs when the service is used or polled. Only your account can retrieve its reports through the website.</p><p>Reports can contain URL query parameters. Review downloaded files before sharing; downloaded copies remain on your device. The six browser-only Tools continue to process inputs locally.</p><p><a class="ovla-download" href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/privacy-policy/')); ?>">Privacy policy →</a> <a class="ovla-download" href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/terms/')); ?>">Terms →</a> <a class="ovla-download" href="https://github.com/Open-ViST/recipe-library/tree/main/projects/link-auditor">Code, documentation and limits ↗</a></p></section></main>
